kmsro pairs a KMS-only device with the SGX545 under powervr_sgx: a scanout
buffer is the GPU's, exported to the display device (a linear render target).

powervr_sgx is a PCI device (the CE5300's SGX is its own PCI function;
Cedarview's sits behind gma500's), so a platform display device (simpledrm on
the EA's boot framebuffer) has to find its render node off the platform bus:
render nodes of PCI devices are taken when their driver is powervr_sgx.

